+## ABI and source
+
+The retained exact1118B parent source is `28F7840..28F7C9E`, SHA256
+`c115401592983d13238154255b9b2583fe85222089d71fde10f0e8aae6c9753c`,
+from the CK31.20.0.4/build25734779 EXE
+`98702f88a547cde2eaf29a85f93b85f68ee4cf8148336a4f7afaeb75319dd518`.
+The source index and complete disassembly are pinned in the prepared contract.
+The new Python checks rebuild this retained source from its six original small
+source spans, verify every span SHA and every disassembly byte, without reading
+an EXE or making a new disassembly/export/xref scan.
+
+RDX is the selected Character pointer, RCX is the task's inline context and R8d
+is the selected index. Original R9 is overwritten before use. The body loads its
+XMM0..3 values from context; its epilogues preserve different incidental RAX
+values. This is insufficient to declare a C++ return type for all callers.
+There is no guessed original-function typedef or C++ original call.
+
+The entry thunk does not CALL anything, dereference any argument, or touch
+XMM/x87/AVX state. It saves every GPR it uses, the original RBP and a PUSHFQ
+flags image, uses only private stack space below entry RSP, and restores inputs
+before tail-jumping to one static copy of the original16B prefix. The original
+home/stack arguments and caller return slot stay in place. The copied prefix
+executes once then jumps to original `entry+16`; the original function's return
+path and return registers remain untouched. PUSHFQ has its architectural RF/VM
+mask behavior; the expected ordinary debug-free admission is not a claim to
+preserve an injected debugger's transient RF state.
+
+The trampoline prefix has no relative instruction. MASM FRAME directives
+describe RBX/RBP pushes, allocation98h and R14 saved at finalRSP+88h. Its actual
+emitted first16B must match the retained anchor before installation. The thunk
+uses RBP as a frame register across flag restoration. At POPFQ it relies on
+frame-based unwind; POP RBP plus the tail JMP must form a recognized epilogue.
+The tail uses an immutable link-time relocated pointer to the static prefix and
+a RIP-relative indirect memory JMP. The first direct-E9 draft was rejected by
+Root's source review against [Microsoft's x64 epilogue rules](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/build/prolog-and-epilog?view=msvc-170)
+and is retained under `rejected-a01/`; no real OS unwind failure was claimed.
+The prefix's own transfer has the opposite constraint: its original frame is
+still allocated, so a recognized tail epilogue would skip needed unwind codes.
+Independent review rejected the second draft's prefix FF25 using the published
+[Microsoft runtime unwinder](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dotnet/runtime/main/src/coreclr/unwinder/amd64/unwinder.cpp).
+That source remains under `rejected-a02/`. The current prefix saves/restores R11
+in private outgoing shadow slots RSP+10h/+08h, then explicitly emits non-REX.W
+`FF 64 24 08` (ModRM01 JMP [RSP+08h]). It preserves GPRs, RSP and native-prefix
+flags; those two slots are below original entryRSP and are not read by the held
+parent body. This avoids the inspected Version1 epilogue patterns at that PC.
+It is an inference from the published algorithm, still awaiting real Windows
+unwind tests and emitted pdata/code verification.
+**This is a design awaiting actual MSVC assembly and RtlVirtualUnwind cold at
+every instruction boundary, including both sides of POPFQ.** Python's source
+stack model cannot qualify Windows unwind, SEH, CET/CFG or emitted code.
